 # Opacity Rendering with SH Colors
-
-
 ## Overview
-This method performs a rendering pass that utilizes the model's actual opacity values while precomputing colors from Spherical Harmonics (SH) coefficients in Python before rasterization, allowing the rasterizer to operate with precomputed RGB colors instead of SH coefficients [S1, unofficial]. It is distinguished from standard SH rendering by moving the SH-to-RGB conversion out of the differentiable rasterization kernel and into the pre-processing stage, effectively treating the Gaussian splats as opaque or alpha-blended entities with fixed colors for the rasterization step [S1, unofficial]. This approach is typically used when the SH degree is not required to be differentiable during the rasterization pass or when simplifying the gradient flow to colors [S1, unofficial].
-
+This method performs a rendering pass that uses the model's actual opacity values and precomputes colors from Spherical Harmonics (SH) in Python before rasterization, allowing the rasterizer to use precomputed colors [S1, unofficial]. It differs from standard SH rendering by performing the SH-to-RGB conversion in the Python host code rather than precomputing colors for the rasterizer, allowing the rasterizer to use simpler color inputs while deferring the directional color evaluation to the CPU/GPU Python layer [S1, unofficial]. The source description states that colors are precomputed from SH, but the provided code initializes the color tensor to ones, indicating a potential implementation simplification or external precomputation step [S1, unofficial].
