 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-- **Gradient Retention:** `screenspace_points` must retain gradients for backpropagation to position parameters. If `retain_grad()` fails (e.g., in older PyTorch versions), it is caught and ignored [S1, unofficial].
-- **Covariance Computation:** The method branches based on `pipeline.compute_cov3D_python`. If `True`, covariances are computed in Python; otherwise, scales and rotations are used directly. This affects memory and speed [S1, unofficial].
-- **Color Initialization:** The source initializes colors to ones. If SH colors are required, this must be replaced with actual SH evaluation. Using ones will result in a white (or background-colored) image if opacity is high [S1, unofficial].
-- **Inference Mode:** The source snippet uses `inference=True`, which may disable gradient computation for speed [S1, unofficial].
